    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-7",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-7",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Left knee pain and reported symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Left anterior/medial knee ache described as a bruise under the kneecap, beginning approximately 2–3 weeks after lifting boxes during a big weekend. Pain 3–4/10 at baseline, up to 6/10 on stairs, especially descending. Worse with stairs, squatting, and standing from a chair after prolonged sitting; settles with rest. No night pain and no significant morning stiffness over 10 minutes. No clear trauma, true locking, giving way, or catching. Patient is unsure whether there is swelling, describing possible evening puffiness. Fully weight-bearing and mobilising unaided; no previous similar episode."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-8",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Left knee examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "No obvious swelling, erythema, or deformity. Mild tenderness at the medial patellar margin and medial patellofemoral joint; no effusion. Full range of motion with mild anterior pain on deep flexion. McMurray test negative; ligaments stable, including to varus and valgus stress. Patellar grind reproduces symptoms. Normal gait; able to partial squat with anterior knee pain."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-9",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-9",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Neck pain and associated symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Central/right paracervical ache described as tight muscles for approximately 6 weeks, with occasional brief sharp twinge on sudden turning. Worse with prolonged desk work, looking down at phone, and driving; better with heat, stretching, ibuprofen, and lying down. No arm pain, paraesthesia, weakness, clumsiness, gait change, bowel or bladder symptoms, or trauma. Sleep somewhat disturbed by waking to change position."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-10",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-10",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Neck examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Normal alignment; no deformity. Increased tone and tenderness in upper trapezius and paracervical muscles, right greater than left. No midline cervical spine tenderness. Mildly reduced bilateral rotation with pain at end range; flexion and extension near full. Spurling test negative. Upper-limb power 5/5 across all myotomes; light-touch sensation intact; biceps, triceps, and brachioradialis reflexes 2+ and symmetrical. Gait normal."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-11",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-11",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "General examination and affect"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Well, no acute distress, talkative and tangential, requiring refocusing several times. Mood described as 'a bit cranky'; denies low mood, anhedonia, and anxiety. No peripheral stigmata of inflammatory arthritis."
      }
    },
